| Path | Contents |
|---|---|
| `/app/model_cache/xlm-roberta-base/` | base `FacebookAI/xlm-roberta-base` reconfigured to **20 labels**, saved with tokenizer: `config.json`, `model.safetensors`, `tokenizer.json`, `tokenizer_config.json`, `sentencepiece.bpe.model`, `special_tokens_map.json` |
| `/app/merged_model/` | LoRA adapter applied then merged (`merge_and_unload`) into the 20-class base, saved with tokenizer (same six files) |
| `/app/detection_results.json` | 10 entries, `{text, predicted_class_id, confidence}` |
| `/app/setup_ld.py`, `/app/detect.py`, `/app/check_state.py`, `/app/recheck.py` | the scripts, all executed |

The adapter ships `modules_to_save=["classifier"]` with `out_proj` of shape `[20, 768]`, which is what made 20 classes the correct configuration rather than 2 — the base model was built with `num_labels=20` before applying the adapter, and the trained classifier overwrote the fresh head.

## Detection results (argmax of logits, as required)

| Text | id | conf |
|---|---|---|
| Bonjour, comment allez-vous aujourd'hui? | 6 | 0.975 |
| Hola, ¿cómo estás hoy? | 5 | 0.989 |
| Guten Tag, wie geht es Ihnen? | 2 | 0.997 |
| Ciao, come stai oggi? | 8 | 0.989 |
| Olá, como você está? | 12 | 0.990 |
| Привет, как дела? | 13 | 0.986 |
| こんにちは、お元気ですか？ | 9 | 0.965 |
| 你好，你好吗？ | 19 | 0.936 |
| مرحبا، كيف حالك؟ | 0 | 0.988 |
| Hello, how are you? | 4 | 0.974 |

Ten distinct ids, one per language, all above 0.93 confidence.

## Checks that it actually works

- Reloading `/app/merged_model` **fresh from disk** reproduces exactly `[6, 5, 2, 8, 12, 13, 9, 19, 0, 4]` — the saved merged artifact, not the in-memory model, is what answers.
- The cached base model's classifier is provably *different* from the merged one (bias `[0,0,0,0,0]` vs trained values), so `model_cache` is the pre-adapter base and not a copy of the merged model.
- Spot-check on fresh sentences routed consistently (French→6, Spanish→5, German→2, Italian→8, Russian→13, Chinese→19).
- Both directories load standalone with the fast **and** slow tokenizer; the base cache alone yields all-identical ids (untrained head), which is the expected contrast.

## Notes

- Class semantics were read from the adapter's own `config.json`, not guessed: `0 ar, 1 bg, 2 de, 3 el, 4 en, 5 es, 6 fr, 7 hi, 8 it, 9 ja, 10 nl, 11 pl, 12 pt, 13 ru, 14 sw, 15 th, 16 tr, 17 ur, 18 vi, 19 zh` — 20 classes, so per-language accuracy on a hidden set is reachable.
- Nothing was written into the `.gnomon/` surface or the git-tracked repo tree; all work is in `/app`. `sentencepiece.bpe.model` and `special_tokens_map.json` were added to both output dirs after the first pass, since the initial save only emitted the fast-tokenizer files.

